<% content_for :title, "Free printable daily checklist for caring for a parent" %>
<% content_for :description, "A one-page daily checklist for caring for an aging parent at home: medication, meals, hydration, appointments, mood and home safety. Print it free, no signup." %>

<div class="no-print">
  <h1>A daily checklist for caring for a parent</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    Most caregiving is not hard, it is just endless — and the worry is usually
    not that you cannot do it, but that you have forgotten something. This is one
    page of the things worth casting an eye over. Print it, put it somewhere you
    pass daily, and let it hold the list instead of your head.
  </p>

  <p>
    Nothing here needs doing in order, and not every line matters every day. It
    is a prompt, not an exam paper.
  </p>

  <p>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" onclick="window.print()">Print this checklist</button>
    <span class="print-hint">or press Ctrl+P — ⌘P on a Mac.</span>
  </p>

  <hr class="rule">
</div>

<%#
  Everything below prints: no navigation, no calls to action. The print rules in
  the marketing layout hide the header, footer and .no-print blocks.
%>
<section class="sheet">
  <h2 class="sheet-title">Daily checklist for <span class="fill fill-name"></span></h2>
  <p class="sheet-week">Week beginning <span class="fill fill-name"></span></p>

  <h3 class="sheet-heading">Morning</h3>
  <ul class="checklist">
    <li>Up, dressed, and moving about</li>
    <li>Morning medication taken</li>
    <li>Breakfast eaten — not just tea</li>
    <li>Hearing aid in, glasses on, batteries working</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="sheet-heading">Through the day</h3>
  <ul class="checklist">
    <li>Something to drink at least every few hours</li>
    <li>A proper meal at midday</li>
    <li>Midday medication, if there is one</li>
    <li>Out of the chair — a walk, the garden, the stairs</li>
    <li>Spoke to somebody other than you</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="sheet-heading">Evening</h3>
  <ul class="checklist">
    <li>Evening meal eaten</li>
    <li>Evening medication taken</li>
    <li>Doors locked, heating set</li>
    <li>Anything needed in the night within reach</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="sheet-heading">Worth a look once a week</h3>
  <ul class="checklist">
    <li>Enough medication left — reorder before it runs low, not after</li>
    <li>Appointments coming up, and who is taking them</li>
    <li>Food in date; anything gone off in the fridge</li>
    <li>Post opened, bills paid</li>
    <li>Phone and any medical devices charged</li>
    <li>Nothing new to trip over — rugs, wires, boxes on the stairs</li>
    <li>Washing done; enough clean clothes</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="sheet-heading">How they seem</h3>
  <p class="sheet-note">
    The part no list can tick for you. Worth writing down when something is
    different, because a pattern is far easier to see on paper than to remember
    across three weeks.
  </p>
  <table class="sheet-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Date</th><th>Something that seemed different</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% 3.times do %>
        <tr><td class="fill"></td><td class="fill"></td></tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>

</section>

<div class="no-print">
  <hr class="rule">

  <p>
    There is also a <a href="<%= routine_sheet_path %>">printable daily routine
    sheet</a> for medication times and contacts, if the routine itself is what
    needs writing down.
  </p>

  <p>
    If keeping the day on track turns into its own job,
    <a href="<%= login_path %>">Remindly</a> speaks reminders aloud at your
    parent's end and tells you what was done and what was missed — so the
    checking does not have to be another phone call. It is free.
  </p>

  <%= render "shared/subscribe_form", source: "caregiver_checklist" %>
</div>
